SUMMARY:Door 1: Lock the front door
DESCRIPTION:DO: Turn on multi-factor authentication for email\, banking and
  work — passkeys or an authenticator app first.\nDON’T: Approve a sign
 -in prompt you didn’t start. A flood of prompts is an attack\, not a gli
 tch.\n\nLesson learnt (Change Healthcare\, Feb 2024): Attackers used stole
 n credentials on a remote-access portal that had no MFA. The ransomware at
 tack disrupted US healthcare payments and exposed data on about 190 millio
 n people.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdven
 t2026/?day=1&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=1&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 1 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-02-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261202T073000Z
DTEND:20261202T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 2: Length beats complexity
DESCRIPTION:DO: Use long passphrases and a password manager — one unique 
 password for every account.\nDON’T: Reuse passwords. IT: don’t force s
 cheduled resets — require a change when there’s evidence of compromise
 .\n\nLesson learnt (23andMe\, Oct 2023): Credential stuffing with reused p
 asswords opened about 14\,000 accounts — and\, through a sharing feature
 \, exposed profile data of about 6.9 million users.\n\nOpen the door: http
 s://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=2&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=2&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 2 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-03-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261203T073000Z
DTEND:20261203T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 3: Think before you paste
DESCRIPTION:DO: Use your organisation’s approved AI tools for work\, with
  data-protection settings switched on.\nDON’T: Paste customer data\, pas
 swords\, source code or contracts into public chatbots.\n\nLesson learnt (
 Samsung\, Apr 2023): Engineers pasted confidential source code and meeting
  notes into a public chatbot. Weeks later\, Samsung restricted generative 
 AI tools on company devices.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.git
 hub.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=3&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=3&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 3 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
