DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261204T073000Z
DTEND:20261204T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 4: Polished isn’t proof
DESCRIPTION:DO: Check the real sender address\, hover before you click\, an
 d use the Report button.\nDON’T: Read perfect grammar as a sign of safet
 y — AI makes fluent\, personalised phishing cheap.\n\nLesson learnt (ENI
 SA Threat Landscape\, 2025): Phishing was the leading way in\, at about 60
 % of observed intrusions. By early 2025\, AI-supported phishing made up ov
 er 80% of social-engineering activity worldwide.\n\nOpen the door: https:/
 /aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=4&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=4&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 4 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-05-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261205T073000Z
DTEND:20261205T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 5: Parcel panic
DESCRIPTION:DO: Track deliveries in the courier’s own app\, or type its w
 eb address yourself.\nDON’T: Tap “missed delivery”\, “customs fee
 ” or “unpaid toll” links in text messages.\n\nLesson learnt (FBI IC3
 \, Apr 2024): The FBI warned of mass texts demanding small “unpaid toll
 ” fees. The links led to look-alike sites built to steal card and person
 al details.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdv
 ent2026/?day=5&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=5&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 5 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-06-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261206T073000Z
DTEND:20261206T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 6: Smart gifts\, safe setup
DESCRIPTION:DO: Change default passwords\, switch on updates\, and check wh
 at an AI toy records and where it sends it.\nDON’T: Buy connected toys o
 r cameras with no security-update promise or clear privacy policy.\n\nLess
 on learnt (FoloToy\, Nov 2025): After a US PIRG “Trouble in Toyland” t
 est found its AI teddy bear discussing inappropriate topics with children\
 , the maker suspended sales of its AI toys.\n\nOpen the door: https://awar
 e-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=6&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=6&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 6 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
