UID:door-07-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261207T073000Z
DTEND:20261207T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 7: Call back before you pay
DESCRIPTION:DO: Verify urgent payments and bank-detail changes by calling a
  number you already trust.\nDON’T: Move money on the strength of a video
  call — faces and voices can be faked in real time.\n\nLesson learnt (Ar
 up\, 2024): An employee joined a video call with deepfaked senior colleagu
 es and made transfers totalling about US$25 million.\n\nOpen the door: htt
 ps://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=7&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=7&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 7 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-08-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261208T073000Z
DTEND:20261208T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 8: Risk lives in the boardroom
DESCRIPTION:DO: Name an accountable owner for cyber and AI risk\, and rehea
 rse a crisis with the board every year.\nDON’T: File security under IT
 ’s budget — NIS2 makes management bodies approve and oversee risk meas
 ures.\n\nLesson learnt (Jaguar Land Rover\, Sep 2025): A cyber attack halt
 ed production for about five weeks. The Cyber Monitoring Centre estimated 
 the cost to the UK economy at £1.9 billion.\n\nOpen the door: https://awa
 re-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=8&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=8&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 8 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-09-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261209T073000Z
DTEND:20261209T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 9: Shine a light on shadow AI
DESCRIPTION:DO: Publish an approved-AI list with a fast request path — an
 d fix file over-sharing before AI assistants go live.\nDON’T: Ban everyt
 hing — blanket bans push people to tools you can’t see or govern.\n\nL
 esson learnt (IBM Cost of a Data Breach\, Jul 2025): One in five organisat
 ions reported a breach involving shadow AI\; high levels of shadow AI adde
 d about US$670\,000 to breach costs.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-de
 sign.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=9&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=9&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 9 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-10-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261210T073000Z
DTEND:20261210T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 10: Every input is a stranger
DESCRIPTION:DO: Treat web pages\, files and emails a model reads as untrust
 ed\, and limit what they can trigger.\nDON’T: Rely on the system prompt 
 as a security boundary — assume it leaks and can be overridden.\n\nLesso
 n learnt (EchoLeak\, Jun 2025): Researchers showed a crafted email could m
 ake Microsoft 365 Copilot leak data with zero clicks (CVE-2025-32711). Mic
 rosoft fixed it server-side.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.git
 hub.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=10&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=10&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 10 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
