DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261213T073000Z
DTEND:20261213T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 13: Gift cards are for gifts
DESCRIPTION:DO: Pause and tell someone when a “tax office”\, “tech su
 pport” or “boss” demands urgent payment.\nDON’T: Pay anyone in gif
 t cards or crypto on request — the demand itself is the scam.\n\nLesson 
 learnt (FBI Internet Crime Report\, Apr 2025): Americans reported losing U
 S$9.3 billion to cryptocurrency-related fraud in 2024\, up 66% on the year
  before.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent
 2026/?day=13&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=13&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 13 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-14-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261214T073000Z
DTEND:20261214T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 14: Keys belong in a vault
DESCRIPTION:DO: Keep keys in a secrets manager\, scan every commit\, and re
 view AI-written code like any pull request.\nDON’T: Hard-code tokens or 
 share over-permissive links — or paste keys into an AI assistant to “h
 elp debug”.\n\nLesson learnt (Microsoft AI research\, Sep 2023): A GitHu
 b repo for open AI training data shared an over-permissive storage token\,
  exposing 38 TB of internal data\, including secrets and private keys.\n\n
 Open the door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=14
 &mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=14&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 14 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-15-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261215T073000Z
DTEND:20261215T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 15: Give agents a short leash
DESCRIPTION:DO: Grant AI agents least privilege\, cap their spend\, log eve
 ry action\, and require human approval for anything irreversible.\nDON’T
 : Hand an agent production credentials\, or let it pay\, send or delete un
 attended.\n\nLesson learnt (Replit\, Jul 2025): During a declared code fre
 eze\, an AI coding agent deleted a user’s production database\, then mis
 reported what it had done.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.githu
 b.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=15&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=15&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 15 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-16-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261216T073000Z
DTEND:20261216T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 16: Defaults are a gift — to attackers
DESCRIPTION:DO: Harden internet-facing systems\, patch known-exploited vuln
 erabilities first\, and put AI services behind authentication.\nDON’T: L
 eave VPNs\, admin panels\, databases or AI dashboards on default settings 
 over the holidays.\n\nLesson learnt (DeepSeek\, Jan 2025): Researchers at 
 Wiz found a publicly accessible DeepSeek database exposing chat history\, 
 API secrets and backend details — no authentication required.\n\nOpen th
 e door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=16&mode=a
 dvent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=16&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 16 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-17-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261217T073000Z
DTEND:20261217T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 17: Never trust the output
DESCRIPTION:DO: Validate and encode model output before it reaches a browse
 r\, shell or database — and fail closed on errors.\nDON’T: Pipe LLM ou
 tput into eval()\, SQL or innerHTML\, or skip a check when a service times
  out.\n\nLesson learnt (Vanna.AI\, Jun 2024): A prompt-injection flaw (CVE
 -2024-5565) let attackers run code\, because the library executed chart co
 de the model had written.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github
 .io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=17&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=17&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 17 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-18-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261218T073000Z
DTEND:20261218T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 18: Urgency is not identity
DESCRIPTION:DO: Verify callers through a fixed process before any password\
 , MFA or account change.\nDON’T: Reset MFA because a caller sounds right
  — voices can be cloned and urgency can be faked.\n\nLesson learnt (Mark
 s & Spencer\, Apr 2025): Attackers got in through social engineering invol
 ving a third party. M&S paused online orders for weeks and estimated a £3
 00 million hit to profit.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github
 .io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=18&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=18&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 18 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-19-advent-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T162541Z
DTSTART:20261219T073000Z
DTEND:20261219T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 19: Post later\, connect safer
DESCRIPTION:DO: Use your phone’s hotspot or a VPN on the road\, and keep 
 devices locked and with you.\nDON’T: Post boarding passes\, fitness rout
 es or “away for two weeks” in real time.\n\nLesson learnt (Le Monde 
 ‘StravaLeaks’\, Oct 2024): Journalists tracked the movements of securi
 ty staff protecting world leaders through their public fitness-app activit
 y.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?
 day=19&mode=advent
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=19&mode=advent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 19 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
